## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design production-ready, self-healing inference pipelines, with drift detection and safe rollback in TF Serving.

## Key Concepts

- Drift metrics: KL divergence on input features and model-proxy accuracy/latency proxies
- Canary rollout and automatic rollback
- Per-model baselines, rolling windows, alerting, and audit logs

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for drift check and rollback trigger
function evaluateDrift(model, payload) {
  const dist = klDivergence(payload.features, model.baseline);
  const lat = measureLatency(model);
  const acc = approximateAccuracy(model, payload.labels);
  return (dist > model.driftThreshold) || (lat > model.latencyThreshold) || (acc < model.accuracyLowerBound);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to set drift thresholds? How to test rollback safely? How to handle cascading rollbacks across models?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of production-grade model serving, stateful components, and zero-downtime updates under streaming data.

## Key Concepts

- Embedding sharding and stateful serving
- Online updates without stale reads
- Atomic model version swaps and canary deployment
- Observability, SLAs, rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: versioned embedding cache lookup
const version = process.env.MODEL_VERSION || 'v1';
const embedCache = loadEmbeddingCache(version);

function predict(inputIds) {
  const emb = embedCache.lookup(inputIds);
  return model.apply(emb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test zero-downtime swap guarantees?
- What race conditions could arise and how would you mitigate them?
